<%# See EnvironmentHelper for why this is staging-only and why it is chrome rather than content. %>
<% if environment_ribbon? %>
  <%# z-60, above the drawers, which are z-50.

      Measured, not assumed: at z-50 the ribbon *already* stays on top of an open mobile drawer,
      because it is later in the DOM. That is exactly the tie design.md's stacking section calls
      fragile - it holds only until somebody reorders the layout - and the remedy it gives is an
      explicit rank rather than a dependence on document order. A statement about which deployment
      you are looking at outranks a panel, so say so in the z-index. %>
  <div class="fixed top-0 left-0 z-60 flex h-8 w-full items-center justify-center gap-2 bg-amber-100 px-4 text-xs font-medium text-amber-900"
       role="status"
       data-testid="environment-ribbon">
    <%= lucide_icon "triangle-alert", class: "size-4 shrink-0", aria: { hidden: true } %>
    <span>Staging &mdash; this is not the real site, and nothing here affects real students</span>
  </div>
<% end %>
